# 0.4 (backlog 52): `state` DERIVES its geometry — rounded — the way
# `decision` derives diamond, because a statechart node has exactly one kind
# and the directive is therefore the whole model (`GENRE-NODE-SPELLING`). Before this release
# `state` fell through to the core `box` default, which made the genre's own
# `SHAPE-ENUM-VOCABULARY` rule ("do not encode state-ness in a shape — the genre already says it")
# unfollowable: obeying it drew the right-angle rectangle ISO 5807 gives to a
# process, so every shipped figure wrote `shape=rounded` on every line.
#
# The second half is the flowchart precedent (fixture 221) held for this
# genre: an explicit `shape=` still overrides the DRAWING ONLY (core §12.7).
# `boxy` below is a state drawn as a box; it is not a process, and the model
# records no role for it — because `state` never records one.
figdown 0.2 statechart
state derived "DERIVED"
state boxy    "OVERRIDDEN" shape=box
state elly    "ELLIPSE"    shape=ellipse
transition derived -[e1]-> boxy
transition boxy -[e2]-> elly
